---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import homeData from '../data/home.json';
---

<Layout
  title="How I built this | GAMER SABBIR"
  personName={homeData.name}
  description="How this portfolio was built with Astro, Tailwind, and live Free Fire tools."
  siteUrl={homeData.siteUrl}
  lang="en"
  socials={homeData.socials}
>
  <section class="section-container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="font-mono text-accent text-xs tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">CHANGELOG</p>
    <h1 class="font-heading font-bold text-4xl text-maintext mb-4">How I built this</h1>
    <p class="text-subtext font-body leading-relaxed mb-8">
      This site is a solo build: a fast static portfolio on GitHub Pages, with live tools visitors can actually use.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-subtext font-body leading-relaxed">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-accent/5 p-5">
        <h2 class="text-maintext font-heading font-bold text-lg mb-2">Stack</h2>
        <p>Astro + Tailwind CSS + TypeScript. Hosted on GitHub Pages. No heavy React app — pages ship as static HTML.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-accent/5 p-5">
        <h2 class="text-maintext font-heading font-bold text-lg mb-2">Live tools</h2>
        <p>Free Fire Info Checker and Like Sender talk to my own APIs. Anyone can type a UID. Likes are limited to 1 per UID per day by the API.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-accent/5 p-5">
        <h2 class="text-maintext font-heading font-bold text-lg mb-2">Why this way</h2>
        <p>I want the portfolio to prove I ship: APIs, bots, and a site people can click around — not just screenshots.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/" class="px-5 py-2 rounded-full bg-accent/20 border border-accent/40 text-maintext text-sm font-semibold">Back home</a>
      <a href="/devtools" class="px-5 py-2 rounded-full border border-white/10 text-subtext text-sm">Dev tools</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
